From 7aa418396ea98aad405ad8b84f3e92b95e790882 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] button: qcom-pmic: keep the function of any other key
 code

A power key that Linux's device tree gives a code other than the ones
the driver remaps (KEY_POWER, KEY_SCREENLOCK ...) used to end up with
no code at all. Such a key now keeps its own code, so the power key
selects (KEY_ENTER) in the boot menu.
---
 drivers/button/button-qcom-pmic.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/button/button-qcom-pmic.c b/drivers/button/button-qcom-pmic.c
index b823490d6d5..3c15fb97d10 100644
--- a/drivers/button/button-qcom-pmic.c
+++ b/drivers/button/button-qcom-pmic.c
@@ -155,6 +155,11 @@ static int qcom_pwrkey_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 			priv->code = KEY_UP;
 			uc_plat->label = "Volume Up";
 			break;
+		default:
+			/* any other code (a power key Linux uses as KEY_POWER, KEY_SCREENLOCK ...)
+			 * keeps the key's own function here: the power key selects (KEY_ENTER) */
+			priv->code = btn_data->code;
+			break;
 		}
 	}
 
